Found under k301 (2026-10-31). lib/OCP/Cmd/Update.pm (~line 177) prints "Manual steps required. Continue? [y/N]: " on STDOUT and reads <STDIN> with no terminal check. A piped `y` confirms. Ctrl-D gives "uninitialized value in chomp". /^y/i also takes "yep" or "yikes".

The precedents just landed: `ocp node trust-host` (k293, d5baab2) and `ocp destroy` (k301). Each has an `_interactive` attribute (-t STDIN, which tests can set) and a `_confirmed` method. Without a terminal they read nothing, say on STDERR what is needed, and exit 1. The question goes to STDERR. Only y/yes (trimmed, case-insensitive) counts; EOF is a no.

Done =
- update behaves the same: a terminal or the non-interactive switch it has (check: --yes/--force; if it has none, say so on the card rather than inventing one);
- tests for a piped y, a closed STDIN, and a terminal stand-in;
- a Changes bullet.
- With three users, move `_interactive`/`_confirmed` into OCP::Role::Cmd (a parameterised message) and switch TrustHost and Destroy to it, with no behaviour change: their tests t/171 and t/301 stay green unchanged.

